      "text": "Sharp instincts and skilled K9 teams at U.S. Border Patrol Checkpoints in New Mexico and Texas led to two major drug seizures.\n\nLas Cruces, NM- Agents at the I-25 checkpoint uncovered 42 bundles of fentanyl pills during a K9 inspection. The drugs weighed 63 lbs. with an estimated value of $2.8 MILLION.\n\nEl Paso, TX- At the Highway 54 Checkpoint, agents noticed a U.S. citizen displaying suspicious behavior. A following K-9 alert led to the discovery of 7 bundles of cocaine, weighing 16+ lbs. and worth approximately $543K.\n\nBoth smugglers now face prosecution for 21USC841- possession of a controlled substance.",
